<title>MALAYSIA: Berjaya Industrial extends year losses.</title>
<headline>Berjaya Industrial extends year losses.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to April 30, 1997</p>
<p>		     (In million ringgit unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net losses    loss    37.79	   vs  loss    24.72</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)   loss     7.4	    vs  loss     4.9</p>
<p>    Turnover	     1,209.75	   vs	 2,351.05</p>
<p>    Minorities    loss    51.21	   vs  loss    74.32</p>
<p>    Extraordinary loss    97.44	   vs  profit 209.87</p>
<p>NOTE - Berjaya Industrial Bhd, part of a major conglomerate, is involved  in real estate, property development and hotels business. The results  are unaudited.</p>
<p>The company said rise in losses was due to fall in dividend income  from subsidiaries and loss of Berjaya Land's contribution, which was  divested in October last year.</p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603-201 4813)</p>
</text>
